gonna be three, comma, three.

01:50.226 --> 01:54.179
So maybe it's right over
there, three, comma, three,

01:54.179 --> 01:57.663
and the curve might look
something like this,

01:57.663 --> 02:00.746
so it might look something like that,

02:02.045 --> 02:04.693
so if you think about
the slope of the line

02:04.693 --> 02:07.055
that connects these two points,

02:07.055 --> 02:10.722
so this line that
connects those two points,

02:12.058 --> 02:14.199
all the mean value theorem,

02:14.199 --> 02:15.972
I'm doing a different color.

02:15.972 --> 02:18.648
All the mean value
theorem tells us is that

02:18.648 --> 02:21.967
there's a point between
one and three where

02:21.967 --> 02:25.238
the slope of the tangent line
has the exact same slope.

02:25.238 --> 02:26.945
So if I were to eyeball it,

02:26.945 --> 02:28.789
it looks like it's right around there,

02:28.789 --> 02:31.299
although we are actually
going to solve for it.

02:31.299 --> 02:34.032
So, some point where the
slope of the tangent line

02:34.032 --> 02:36.381
is equal to the slope of the line

02:36.381 --> 02:38.614
that connects these two end points

02:38.614 --> 02:41.806
and their corresponding function values.

02:41.806 --> 02:46.180
So that is c, that would
be c right over there.

02:46.180 --> 02:48.863
So really we just have to solve this.

02:48.863 --> 02:51.828
So let's first just find
out what f prime of x is,

02:51.828 --> 02:54.590
and then we could substitute a c in there

02:54.590 --> 02:57.553
and then we can evaluate
this on the right hand side.

02:57.553 --> 02:59.886
So I'm gonna rewrite f of x,

03:01.522 --> 03:04.624
f of x is equal to, and I'm gonna write it

03:04.624 --> 03:08.869
as four x to the minus
three to the one half power.

03:08.869 --> 03:10.937
Makes it a little bit more
obvious that we can apply

03:10.937 --> 03:13.247
the power rule and the chain rule here.

03:13.247 --> 03:16.759
So f prime of x is going
to be the derivative

03:16.759 --> 03:19.341
of four x minus three to the one half

03:19.341 --> 03:21.895
with respect to four x minus three,

03:21.895 --> 03:25.227
so that is going to be
one half times four x

03:25.227 --> 03:28.109
minus three to the negative one half,

03:28.109 --> 03:29.910
and then we're gonna multiply that

03:29.910 --> 03:31.906
times the derivative of four x

03:31.906 --> 03:34.112
minus three with respect to x.

03:34.112 --> 03:37.236
Well, derivative of four x
with respect to x is just four,

03:37.236 --> 03:39.718
and the derivative of negative
three with respect to x,

03:39.718 --> 03:41.440
well that's just gonna be zero,

03:41.440 --> 03:43.214
so the derivative of four x minus three

03:43.214 --> 03:45.278
with respect to x is four.

03:45.278 --> 03:46.918
So times four.

03:46.918 --> 03:48.168
so f prime of x

03:50.507 --> 03:53.174
is equal to four times one half,

03:55.144 --> 03:59.311
which is two, over the square
root of four x minus three.

04:01.483 --> 04:03.763
Four x minus three to the one half

04:03.763 --> 04:05.786
would just be the square
root of four x minus three,

04:05.786 --> 04:07.319
but it's the negative one half,

04:07.319 --> 04:09.590
so we're gonna put it in the
denominator right over here.

04:09.590 --> 04:12.759
And so f prime of c, we could rewrite this

04:12.759 --> 04:16.926
